1)Recreate Strategy:-
-----------------------
*)✅ No version conflict – The old pods are completely deleted before new pods start, so only one version of the application runs at a time, avoiding compatibility issues

Old Pods Running (v1)
        ↓
All Old Pods Deleted
        ↓
Application Temporarily Down
        ↓
New Pods Created (v2)
        ↓
Application Starts Again


ExAMPLE:-

apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: nginx-deploy
spec:
  replicas: 3

  strategy:
    type: Recreate

  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx

  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: nginx:1.26
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------


2)rooling :-In Kubernetes, the Rolling Update Strategy is used to update an application without downtime. 🚀
It gradually replaces old pods with new pods instead of stopping everything at once.

2)In Kubernetes, the Rolling Update strategy provides zero downtime, meaning the application continues running while old pods are gradually replaced with new pods. 🚀

Old Pods Running (v1)
        ↓
New Pod Created (v2)
        ↓
New Pod Becomes Ready
        ↓
One Old Pod Terminated
        ↓
Repeat Process
        ↓
All Pods Updated to New Version
        ↓
Application Always Available (No Downtime)

✅ Advantage: The application keeps running during the update, so users do not experience downtime. 🚀
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3)Blue-Green Deployment Strategy:-           100%user are impack      
---------------------------------------

Blue-Green deployment means running two identical environments at the same time.

Blue environment → Current running version (production)

Green environment → New version of the application

When the new version is ready, traffic is switched from Blue to Green. 🚀

Blue Environment (v1 running)
        ↓
Green Environment Created (v2)
        ↓
Testing Done on Green
        ↓
Switch Traffic to Green
        ↓
Green Becomes Production

🔹 Key Advantage:-

✅ Instant rollback – If the new version has issues, traffic can quickly switch back to the Blue environment.


------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4)Canary Strategy

Start
  ↓
Develop New Change / Feature
  ↓
Select Small Group of Users (5–10%)
  ↓
Deploy the Change to the Small Group
  ↓
Monitor System Performance & User Feedback
  ↓
Are there any issues?
   ↓            ↓
  YES           NO
   ↓             ↓
Rollback /      Gradually Release
Fix the Issue   to More Users
   ↓             ↓
Improve &       Deploy to All Users
Retest
   ↓             ↓
  End           End


*)The Canary strategy releases a new version of the application to a small number of users first, while most users still use the old version.

If the new version works well, it is gradually rolled out to all users. 🚀

🔹 Advantage

✅ Reduced risk – Only a small group of users test the new version first, so problems can be detected early.


